.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class STP> void \fBcsmp::ExplicitNodeCenteredFiniteVolumeTransport\fP< dim, STP >::AdvectVariable1stOrder (double time_increment, bool output_result_range)\fR [protected]\fP"

.PP
explicit conservative Explicit first-order advection algorithm of a passive conservative tracer\&. AdvectVariableFirstOrder() uses the upstream values of the advected variable to compose the solution in the result \fBvector<double>\fP managed by the ExplicitFiniteVolumeAlgorithm which performs a range check and writes the RESULT back to the \fBModel\fP\&. 
.br
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
Reference to the current model and the ExplicitFiniteVolumeAlgorithm as well as the time_increment for the transport step\&. This increment must fulfill the CFL criterion\&. 
.br
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
The method uses the ExplicitFiniteVolumeProcessor object in the accumulation of the finite-volume stencils, when it loops over the elements\&. 
.br
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
Since it costs almost the same to compute the second-order accurate explicit solution, there is not much rational to use this method\&. 
